# Extra exclusions for the API image only.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile path>.dockerignore` before falling back to the
# context's `.dockerignore`, so this file applies to `-f apps/api/Dockerfile`
# and to nothing else. That is what lets the API build drop the web client —
# which it has no use for — while `apps/web/Dockerfile`, building from the same
# context, still receives it.
#
# When this file is used it REPLACES the root .dockerignore rather than adding
# to it, so the root rules are repeated below. Keep the two in step.
#
# On a builder without BuildKit this file is ignored and the root .dockerignore
# applies instead: the API context is then larger than it needs to be, which
# costs upload time and nothing else. It degrades to slower, never to wrong.

.git
.github
.claude
.gitignore
.dockerignore

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-seed
**/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# The web client is deployed separately (Vercel, or apps/web/Dockerfile).
# This is the one line that differs from the root file.
apps/web

# Docs and local tooling — not required at runtime.
*.md
!apps/api/**/*.md
docker-compose.yml
render.yaml
railway.json
vercel.json

# Tests and editor noise
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.vscode
**/.idea
